<Layout lang="en" title="Alice and the White Rabbit: their first encounter - Castellation" description="Explore how Alice's curiosity and the White Rabbit's hurried appearance begin their connection in the first chapter of Wonderland.">
  <SiteHeader lang="en" />
  <main><article>
    <header class="encounter-hero"><div class="wrap"><a href="/guides">← All reading guides</a><p class="eyebrow">✦ FIRST ENCOUNTERS / CHAPTER ONE</p><h1>Alice &amp; the<br /><em>White Rabbit.</em></h1><p>One curious glance becomes the first thread in a much larger story.</p><div class="diagram" aria-label="Alice follows the White Rabbit"><span>Alice<small>THE OBSERVER</small></span><div>FOLLOWS <b>→</b></div><span>The White Rabbit<small>THE STRANGER</small></span></div></div></header>
    <div class="wrap encounter-article"><aside><p class="eyebrow">READING SCOPE</p><strong>Chapter one</strong><p>This guide stays within the opening of Alice's Adventures in Wonderland.</p><a href="https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/28885/pg28885-images.html">Read the original text ↗</a></aside><div><p class="lead">They have not exchanged a word when Alice decides to follow. The connection begins with a small detail that makes the ordinary suddenly strange.</p><section><h2>What catches Alice's attention?</h2><p>Alice is sitting beside her sister when a White Rabbit runs past, talking to himself about being late. It is his watch, taken from a waistcoat pocket, that makes her jump up and follow him. His hurry gives her curiosity a direction.</p></section><section><h2>A connection without a conversation</h2><p>The Rabbit does not invite Alice along. She chooses to pursue him, and that choice carries her down the rabbit-hole. Their first connection is therefore one of observation and pursuit: the reader sees the Rabbit through the detail Alice notices.</p></section><section><h2>A question to take into the story</h2><p>Which matters more to Alice at this moment: where the Rabbit is going, or the fact that he is so unusual? Keep the question in mind as you read, and let your answer change with the evidence.</p></section><div class="next"><p class="eyebrow">✦ KEEP EXPLORING</p><h2>Follow the story at your own pace.</h2><a class="primary-button" href="/books/alices-adventures-in-wonderland/opening">Explore Alice's first chapter ↗</a><p><a href="/guides/alice-down-the-rabbit-hole">Read the guide to the rabbit-hole ↗</a></p></div></div></div>
  </article></main><SiteFooter lang="en" />
</Layout>
